8. Conclusion

This dissertation has constructed a self‑contained, mathematically rigorous theory of Resonant Physics‑Native Intelligence. By replacing static weights and global optimisation with adaptive, continuous‑time oscillatory dynamics, the RPNI framework offers a radically different paradigm for computation and learning. All central claims—convergence of the plasticity rule, unified criticality, robust associative memory, and scalable storage capacity—have been proved from first principles, using the latest advances in stochastic approximation, random matrix theory, and nonlinear dynamics. The work provides a complete formal specification of an RPNI machine, ready to guide future theoretical extensions and, ultimately, physical realisations in emerging hardware platforms. No experiments or simulations were needed; the mathematics itself is the contribution, a verified blueprint for intelligence that is truly physics‑native.



