Description:
External time‑dependent signals u_k(t) are fed into an input encoder that weights them by a matrix W^{\text{in}} to produce injection currents into the oscillator core. The core is a fully connected network of N Stuart–Landau OCUs, each producing a complex state z_i. The phase variables \theta_i and the order parameter R are extracted continuously. The plasticity module computes fast eligibility traces E_{ij} from pairwise phase differences and updates the coupling weights K_{ij} using the three‑factor rule, gated by the consolidation signal \Gamma(t). The criticality controller monitors the order parameter variance (susceptibility) and avalanche statistics to estimate \widehat{\chi} and \widehat{\sigma}_b, then adjusts a global coupling gain g and forms the gate \Gamma(t) to confine plasticity to the Critical Resonant State. The readout computes a linear combination of \cos\theta_i and \sin\theta_i to produce output signals. All blocks operate in continuous time; no digital clock or discrete iteration is defined.

